# The 32-bit words held as the JVM's int: int32_type under a criterion of its own, so that
# a backend may hold such a word as one int rather than as 32 cells. jvm_int_type is
# int32_type under the synthetic label $int, the identity the label's partial function
# applied to its key is, the two equal by the β rule (docs/design/gezi-set-equations-proofs.md,
# section 25).
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "fixed_width") "int32_representation")
λ _ int32_type _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. (λ"$int" v. v) "$int" int32_type)
λ jvm_int_type
. export jvm_int_type
